cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LC-MS Contaminant Finder"
message: "If you use this resource, please cite it and, where you rely on a specific entry, the original source recorded in that entry's reference field."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Quach
    given-names: Austin
    email: austin.quach@daltonbioanalytics.com
abstract: >-
  A curated, exact-mass-validated compendium of LC-MS contaminant and background
  ions, with a browser-based tool for identifying an unknown ion from its m/z,
  charge state and isotope envelope. Every m/z is recomputed from its molecular
  formula and adduct rather than transcribed. Coverage includes plasticizers,
  cyclic siloxanes, polyethylene glycols and other polymer series, surfactants,
  solvent and salt clusters, labware leachables, stationary-phase bleed and
  metal corrosion products from LC flow paths. Entries carry provenance, the
  homologous-series spacing where applicable, an MS1 specificity estimate, and
  a flag for whether public MS2 spectra exist.
keywords:
  - mass spectrometry
  - LC-MS
  - contaminant
  - background ion
  - metabolomics
  - proteomics
  - blank
  - column bleed
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/aquachdb/lcms-contaminants"
url: "https://aquachdb.github.io/lcms-contaminants/"
